{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[E]Rat in a drain ditch, Caught on a limb,
[A]You know better but [B]I know [E]him
[E]Like I told you, what I said,
[A]Steal your face right [B]off your [E]head
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[E]Now he's [A][E]gone, now he's [A][E]gone, [D]Lord he's [A]gone, he's [B]gone.
Like a [A]steam locomotive, [B]rollin' down the track
He's [A]gone, gone, [E]nothin's gonna [D]bring him [A]back, he's [E]gone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Nine mile skid on a ten mile ride,
Hot as a pistol but cool inside
Cat on a tin roof, dogs in a pile,
Nothin' left to do but smile, smile, smile
{end_of_verse}

